      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مِرْفَاقٌ</span></b>  A camel <i>whose elbow hurts</i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">يُصِيبُ</span>) <i>his
side.</i> (O, K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  And A she-camel <i>that is hurt
by the</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">صِرَار</span> [q. v.] <i>when her udder is bound therewith, and from whom blood issues</i> (JK, O, K)
<i>when she is loosed</i> [<i>therefrom</i>] (<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">إِذَا حُلَّتْ</span>), (JK,)
or <i>when she is milked</i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اذا حُلِبَتْ</span>). (O, K.)

